.TH SAAT 1 "2026-07-29" "SAAT" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
saat \- catalogue a mechanical-watch collection
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B saat
.RI [ --autostart ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B SAAT
is a local, offline desktop application for cataloguing a personal wristwatch
collection. It organises watches into a photo-forward grid, a dense spec
table and a wear calendar, shows a detail page per watch, compares watches
side by side, and records what was worn on which day.
.PP
It ships empty. Every watch is entered by its owner.
.PP
There is no database and no network access: each watch is a plain, editable
TOML file on disk beside its own images, so the collection remains readable
and portable without this program.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-autostart
Signals that this launch came from the XDG autostart entry rather than from
the user. Only meaningful together with the tray menu's
.B Start minimised
option, which must never affect a manual launch. Not intended to be typed by
hand.
.SH FILES
When installed from a package, SAAT uses the standard per-user locations:
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/saat/watches/
One directory per watch, each holding a
.I watch.toml
and an
.I images/
subdirectory.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/saat/backups/
Timestamped copies of
.IR watch.toml ,
written before any destructive change and pruned to the newest 20. Deleted
watches are moved to
.I backups/deleted/
rather than erased.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/saat/sellers.toml
Optional seller directory. Created on first use.
.TP
.I ~/.config/saat/config.toml
Window geometry, the active view, column choices, language and palette.
.PP
Removing or purging the package does not delete any of the above.
.PP
A portable copy of SAAT \(em the tarball from the releases page, extracted
anywhere \(em keeps all of these beside its own executable instead, so the
whole folder can be moved to another machine with the collection intact.
Which mode is in use is decided by a
.I .installed
marker file beside the executable, which only a package or
.I install.sh
creates.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B SAAT_DATA_DIR
Overrides both locations above at once, collapsing data and configuration
into the named directory regardless of installed or portable mode.
.TP
.B XDG_DATA_HOME
.TQ
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
Honoured in installed mode, per the XDG Base Directory specification. SAAT
appends
.I /saat
to each.
